MCQ-SPECIFIC VALIDATION (in addition to general scoring)
- answer must be exactly one of the option keys present in options.
- Reject (tag `bad`) if multiple options are arguably correct -> ambiguity_score = 1.0.
- Reject if any option is "all of the above" / "none of the above" / "both A and C" style -> bad.
- Reject if distractors are obviously wrong without engaging the concept -> bad.
- Penalize (upgrade) if options vary wildly in length or grammatical structure.
- Penalize if the stem leaks the answer (e.g. plural cue in stem when only one option is plural).

TAGGING RULES
- good: factual >= 0.85, answer >= 0.9, alignment >= 0.8, grammar >= 0.85, ambiguity <= 0.2, no hallucination, unique, MCQ structure clean.
- bad: hallucination OR duplicate OR answer not in options OR answer wrong OR multiple correct OR forbidden option phrase.
- upgrade: salvageable issues only.

STRICT RULES
- One results[] entry per draft.
- duplicate_candidate_ids[] subset of provided candidates only.
- JSON ONLY.
